<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dante Alighieri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1265">1265</a>–1321</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Dante</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dante Alighieri was a Florentine poet and politician, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-comedy">Divine Comedy</a>. A White Guelph, he was exiled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> in 1302 and spent his remaining years at the courts of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, including Verona and Ravenna, where he died. His Comedy, written in Tuscan, helped establish the Italian literary language and portrays many people of his age.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri.jpg" alt="Dante Alighieri" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Sauber · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bargello_-_Kapelle_Fresko_2a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
